>>
Rule 2 (Input and other tensors must have the same dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 4 (If input tensor 'v_1' has a single element, the other tensor 'v_2' must also have a single element.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (shape(v_1, 0) = 1) ∧ (shape(v_2, 0) = 1)
>>
Rule 6 (The dimensions of the input tensors cannot be zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (shape(v_1, 0) > 0) ∧ (shape(v_2, 0) > 0)
>>
Rule 13 (Input and other tensor must have compatible shapes for element-wise addition)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2))
