{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 32 (If input tensors have different shapes in a non-singleton dimension, the shapes should be broadcastable.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1))
>>
